      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Make sure that you use the \"Set Standing Height\" instead of playspace mover or OVRAS if you're adjusting how high your head is after locking in your horizon adjustment. If you vertically dragged your playspace around instead, resetting the horizon adjustment in VRC will still have the external playspace offset active in your external software.\nAs for locking in to tilted angles, if you want the horizon adjustment to lock in exactly to your viewpoint angle make sure you deactivate the \"snap\" mode. (Snap mode instead locks to the nearest 90 degree increment)\nCan you confirm that none of the above was the cause of your issues? If so please give some more details and possibly screenshots or videos of how to reproduce the problems. Thanks!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
